A method performed by a first device, the method comprising:

establishing, by the first device, a control structure associated with a Multipath Transmission Control Protocol (MPTCP) session established between the first device and a second device;

maintaining, in the control structure, session information identifying a plurality of Transmission Control Protocol (TCP) subflows associated with the MPTCP session;

for each TCP subflow of the plurality of TCP subflows, tracking, by the first device, subflow state information comprising at least one TCP sequence number associated with data carried on the TCP subflow; and

generating, by the first device, a mapping between the at least one TCP sequence number of each TCP subflow and a globally unique identifier corresponding to data within the MPTCP session,

wherein the globally unique identifier uniquely identifies the data across the plurality of TCP subflows of the MPTCP session.
